Design the system architecture – Decide the overall structure and major components of the system.

Design the user interface – Plan screens, navigation, layouts, and user interactions.

Design the database – Decide what data needs to be stored and how different data items are related.

Design system modules – Divide the project into smaller, manageable modules or components.

Select technologies – Choose suitable programming languages, frameworks, databases, and development tools.

Design workflows – Define how information and processes move through the system.

Create diagrams and models – Use flowcharts, UML diagrams, ER diagrams, wireframes, or other design models.

Plan security and performance – Consider authentication, data protection, scalability, and system performance.
